  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Heads up, I seem to have run across a bug with unity and the new SDK. (VRCSDK-2019.09.18.12.05_Public.unitypackage).\n\nIt seems that if you overwrite the old SDK with the current new one, it breaks dynamic bones on any model in scene causing the dynamic bone script to not be recognized. I tried then deleting the entire VRCSDK folder and importing the new SDK again after that, as well as reimporting the Dynamic Bones script and this seemed to fix the issue but the dynamic bones on the model were reset to default values. This only affected the model that has a loaded scene during the time. My friend experienced the same issue so I figured it may not just be a one time fluke, and that I should inform people just in case.",
